● useContext
------------
It allows components to share data without passing props through every level.
This solves prop drilling.

Very commonly used for:
- Logged-in user
- Theme
- Language
- Authentication information
- Application settings

------------
● useReducer
------------
useReducer అనేది React లో state management కోసం ఉపయోగించే Hook. 
దీన్ని ఉపయోగించి మనం component లోని state ని manage చేయవచ్చు.
dispatch ద్వారా actions పంపుతాం, reducer function ఆ actions ఆధారంగా కొత్త state ని return చేస్తుంది. 
dispatch అనేది reducer function కి action ని పంపడానికి ఉపయోగించే function.
Complex state management కోసం ఇది ఉపయోగపడుతుంది.
ముఖ్యంగా state changes కొంచెం complex గా ఉన్నప్పుడు ఇది ఉపయోగపడుతుంది.

సింపుల్‌గా చెప్పాలంటే, useState లాగే useReducer కూడా state ని manage చేస్తుంది. 
కానీ state ని మార్చడానికి మనం ఒక reducer function ఉపయోగిస్తాం (OR) State update logic ఒక reducer function లో ఉంటుంది.
Reducer ద్వారా state update చేస్తాం.

useReducer is a React Hook used to manage component state. 
It works with a reducer function and dispatch function. 
We dispatch actions, and the reducer function returns the next state (updated value) based on the action. 
So dispatch is a function is used to send actions to the reducer function to update the state (updated value). 
The new updated state value replaces the current state value.
It is useful when state management logic becomes complex OR when multiple actions update the same state.

It is useful when state logic becomes complex.
It manage complex state logic / Complex state management using actions.

syntax :- const [state, dispatch] = useReducer(reducer, initialState);
state → Current state value, Similar to state in useState.
dispatch → Sends an action to the reducer, Similar in purpose to setState in useState.
reducer → Function that handles state updates based on actions.
initialState → Initial state value.

Very commonly used for:
- Complex Forms: Form values, validation errors, submit status.
- Shopping cart: Add item, remove item, update quantity.
- Multi-step Forms: Next step, previous step, reset.
- Complex UI state
- State with many actions

------
● NOTE
------
useState uses a setter function (setState), whereas useReducer uses a dispatch function (dispatch) to send actions to the reducer.
